# AXIS CELL: scrutinee type = NON-ENUM (int) x consumer = the `safety_commit`
# JOIN in `check_safety_stmt`'s `SMatch` arm. The divergence-gate cell for the
# same scrutinee type is `match_no_catchall_diverge_use_after_move_reject.gg`.
#
# `n` is neither 1 nor 2, so the fall-through path reaches `print(s)` with `s`
# still moved. An int scrutinee has no closed universe of values, so NO
# exhaustiveness verdict -- present or future, one bit or two -- can ever credit
# this match as covering everything. That is what makes the cell load-bearing:
# it stays RED under any fusion of an exhaustiveness verdict into the
# fall-through question, and stays GREEN under the correct second-bit design.
#
# RED-VERIFY (break the JOIN consumer): in self_host_typechecker/typecheck.gg
# replace
#   `safety_commit(m_acc, not match_has_catch_all(arms), m_reached, &state)`
# with `safety_commit(m_acc, false, m_reached, &state)` and rebuild the driver.
# Measured: this cell flips rc 1 -> rc 0, 4293 bytes of C.
void sink(String ^x):
    pass

void probe(int n):
    String s = "hello"
    sink(^s)
    match n:
        case 1:
            s = "a"
        case 2:
            s = "b"
    print(s)

void main():
    probe(3)
